# SH_MAMESOCK_KEYMAP for the host-native `indyr4400` station (Iris).
#
# GENERATED by scripts/dev/iris-keymap.py — do not hand-edit; regenerate.
#
# Columns: browser XT set-1 scancode <TAB> port <TAB> field.
#
# Iris's keyboard is a PS/2 controller, not a scanned matrix, so there is
# exactly ONE port (`kbd`) and the field is a `winit::keyboard::KeyCode`
# variant name — which is also the W3C `KeyboardEvent.code` the SPA sends,
# so this file is very nearly an identity map. `Ps2::push_kb` encodes the
# scancode itself and the guest applies its own `keybd=` layout on top;
# nothing here is IRIX-specific.
#
# Shift/Ctrl/Alt are ordinary rows, not special cases — which is what makes
# both `_` and Ctrl-C work. Caps Lock is deliberately absent (the fork's
# set-1 encoder has no arm for it and would drop the byte silently).

01	kbd	Escape
02	kbd	Digit1
03	kbd	Digit2
04	kbd	Digit3
05	kbd	Digit4
06	kbd	Digit5
07	kbd	Digit6
